{{!
    @template mod_vrroom/editor_assetchooser

    Body of the room editor's "which file?" dialogue for a new 3D model, image or media object:
    one of the activity's files (none chosen at first), or a new upload.

    Data attributes required for JS:
    * data-action="vrroom-chooser-upload"

    Context variables required for this template:
    * id - id of the select
    * options - the files: value (file key), label (file name)

    Example context (json):
    {
        "id": "vrroom-chooser-1",
        "options": [
            {"value": "[\"assets\",1,\"/\",\"vase.glb\"]", "label": "vase.glb"}
        ]
    }
}}
<div class="mb-3">
    <label class="form-label" for="{{id}}">{{#str}}editorchoosefilelabel, mod_vrroom{{/str}}</label>
    <select class="form-select" id="{{id}}">
        <option value="" selected>{{#str}}editorchoosefilenone, mod_vrroom{{/str}}</option>
        {{#options}}
        <option value="{{value}}">{{label}}</option>
        {{/options}}
    </select>
</div>
<p class="mb-0">
    <button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary" data-action="vrroom-chooser-upload">{{#str}}editorupload, mod_vrroom{{/str}}</button>
</p>
